solid-checker-wasm vendors part of @tybys/wasm-util 0.10.3

Files under lib/ are copied from the npm package @tybys/wasm-util at version
0.10.3: the synchronous WASI runtime closure the owned check's worker needs
(lib/mjs/webassembly.mjs, memory.mjs, jspi.mjs and lib/mjs/wasi/index.mjs,
preview1.mjs, path.mjs, types.mjs, fd.mjs, error.mjs, util.mjs, rights.mjs).
UPSTREAM.json records the upstream and owned sha256 of every file and how the
upstream bytes were identified.

Modifications by solid-checker (complete in owned.patch):
- lib/mjs/wasi/physical.mjs is new: physical, component-wise path resolution.
  It exports its substitution bound (MAX_SUBSTITUTIONS) for the owned
  worker's directory store.
- lib/mjs/wasi/preview1.mjs: the synchronous bodies of path_open,
  path_filestat_get, path_readlink, path_create_directory,
  path_remove_directory and path_unlink_file call physical.mjs instead of the
  lexical resolve/resolvePathSync, and path_readlink truncates to the buffer
  instead of returning ENOBUFS; and the synchronous fd_pread, fd_pwrite,
  fd_read and fd_write decode each iovec's buffer address unsigned
  (getUint32, not getInt32), so an address at or above 2 GiB is not read
  relative to the end of memory. Nothing else changed.

